{"name":"One Minute to Midnight","hex":"#003388","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"one","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO & ICAO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the digit 1."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Oneida."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/one"},{"term":"minute","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A unit of time which is one sixtieth of an hour (sixty seconds).","A short but unspecified time period."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Of an event, to write in a memo or the minutes of a meeting.","To set down a short sketch or note of; to jot down; to make a minute or a brief summary of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minute"},{"term":"midnight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The middle of the night: the sixth temporal hour, equidistant between sunset and sunrise.","Twelve o'clock at night exactly."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Utterly dark or black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midnight"}],"entries":[{"title":"One Minute to Midnight","blocks":[{"text":"One Minute to Midnight is a 2026 French drama film written and directed by Nicolas Pariser. It stars Melvil Poupaud, Chiara Mastroianni, Golshifteh Farahani, and Léonie Simaga."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Minute_to_Midnight"},{"title":"Doomsday Clock","blocks":[{"text":"The Doomsday Clock is a symbol that represents the estimated likelihood of a human-made global catastrophe, in the opinion of the nonprofit organization Bulletin of the Atomic Scientists."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Doomsday_clock_%281.42_minutes%29.svg/330px-Doomsday_clock_%281.42_minutes%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doomsday_Clock"},{"title":"One Minute","blocks":[{"text":"\"One Minute\" is a song recorded by American singer Kelly Clarkson taken from her third studio album, My December (2007). The song served as the album's second single in Australia on September 18, 2007, through 19 Recordings and RCA Records. Clarkson originally wrote it for her second studio album, Breakaway (2004), with songwriters Kara DioGuardi, Chantal Kreviazuk and Raine Maida; however, it did not make the final track listing. It was then reworked for My December, being produced by David Kahne, and co-produced by Jason Halbert and Jimmy Messer. \"One Minute\" is an alternative rock song with electropop influences, and consists of \"rapid-fire give-and-take verses\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/88/Clarkson-OneMinute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Minute"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Cast_and_director_of_One_Minute_to_Midnight-0486.jpg/500px-Cast_and_director_of_One_Minute_to_Midnight-0486.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Cast_and_director_of_One_Minute_to_Midnight-0486.jpg/1280px-Cast_and_director_of_One_Minute_to_Midnight-0486.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Cast_and_director_of_One_Minute_to_Midnight-0486.jpg/500px-Cast_and_director_of_One_Minute_to_Midnight-0486.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clara Pacini, Léonie Simaga, Nicolas Pariser, Chiara Mastroianni and Melvil Poupaud at the 83rd Venice International Film Festival","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACast_and_director_of_One_Minute_to_Midnight-0486.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Bulletin_Atomic_Scientists_Cover.jpg/500px-Bulletin_Atomic_Scientists_Cover.jpg?utm_source